  "details": "I've seen them before (but I'm not sure specifically where), but a \"benchmarking graph\" that would allow us to see what is taking up render time in the current view would be very useful in tracking down optimization problems. I'm imagining something that would be like:\n\n1.6ms/12ms - Mesh Renderers\n    xx - Static Mesh rendering\n    xx - Morphed mesh rendering\n\n3.3ms/12ms - Shaders\n    0.9ms - shader1\n     0.5ms - shader2\n\nand so on for lighting, etc etc. I think this would be very useful.\n     etc..",
